@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam stateBackgroundColor MODEL_COLOR_T1
skinparam stateBorderColor MODEL_COLOR
skinparam arrowColor MODEL_COLOR
skinparam stateFontColor #202020

title Logical member record lifecycle (stable NUS ID)

state "Active member\ndeleted = false" as Active
state "Deleted member\ndeleted = true" as Deleted

[*] --> Active
Active --> Active : member edit [valid changed details] /\nreplace details; retain NUS ID
Active --> Deleted : member delete [no outstanding loans] /\ndeleted := true
Deleted --> Active : member restore / deleted := false

note left of Active
  Editing is allowed with outstanding loans.
  Empty and unchanged edits are rejected.
  Outstanding loans block deletion.
  Restoring an active member is rejected.
end note
note right of Deleted
  NUS ID, details and loan history are retained.
  Restoration has no deadline; records are never purged.
  Editing, new loans and repeated deletion are rejected.
  Restore before editing or borrowing again.
end note
note bottom of Active
  Initial entry represents a newly added active record.
  States describe a logical record, not one Java object.
  Edits, deletion and restoration replace immutable Member instances.
  Successful mutations save an isolated snapshot before publishing.
  Validation or save failures leave live state and saved bytes unchanged.
  Archival and deletion timestamps are outside scope.
end note
@enduml
